      "content": "<h3>All ArrayList methods at a glance</h3>\n<p>Each method is explained with its own runnable example in the next tab. <em>n</em> is the number of elements.</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;\">\n<tr><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Method</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">What it does</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Time</th></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>add(e)</strong></td><td>Adds at the end</td><td>O(1) amortised</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>add(i, e)</strong></td><td>Inserts at index i, shifting the rest right</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>addAll(c)</strong> / <strong>addAll(i, c)</strong></td><td>Adds every element of another collection</td><td>O(m) / O(n+m)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>addFirst(e)</strong> / <strong>addLast(e)</strong></td><td>Adds at the start / end (Java 21)</td><td>O(n) / O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>get(i)</strong></td><td>Reads the element at index i</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>getFirst()</strong> / <strong>getLast()</strong></td><td>Reads the first / last element (Java 21)</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>set(i, e)</strong></td><td>Replaces the element at index i, returns the old one</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>size()</strong> / <strong>isEmpty()</strong></td><td>Number of elements / is it empty</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>contains(o)</strong> / <strong>containsAll(c)</strong></td><td>Is the element (all elements) present</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>indexOf(o)</strong> / <strong>lastIndexOf(o)</strong></td><td>First / last position of an element, -1 if missing</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>remove(i)</strong> / <strong>remove(o)</strong></td><td>Removes by index / by value</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>removeFirst()</strong> / <strong>removeLast()</strong></td><td>Removes the first / last element (Java 21)</td><td>O(n) / O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>removeAll(c)</strong> / <strong>retainAll(c)</strong></td><td>Removes / keeps only the elements found in c</td><td>O(n*m)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>removeIf(p)</strong></td><td>Removes every element that matches a condition</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>replaceAll(op)</strong></td><td>Replaces every element with the result of a function</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>sort(cmp)</strong></td><td>Sorts the list in place</td><td>O(n log n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>clear()</strong></td><td>Removes everything</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>subList(a, b)</strong></td><td>A live view of a part of the list</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>toArray()</strong> / <strong>toArray(T[])</strong></td><td>Copies the elements into an array</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>stream()</strong></td><td>Starts a stream pipeline over the elements</td><td>O(1) to create</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>iterator()</strong> / <strong>listIterator()</strong></td><td>Walks the elements (and can remove / add / go backwards)</td><td>O(1) per step</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>forEach(action)</strong> / <strong>spliterator()</strong></td><td>Runs an action for every element / splittable iteration</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>clone()</strong></td><td>Shallow copy of the list</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>equals(o)</strong> / <strong>hashCode()</strong> / <strong>toString()</strong></td><td>Compare, hash and print by content</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>ensureCapacity(n)</strong> / <strong>trimToSize()</strong></td><td>Grow the room ahead / shrink it to fit</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>reversed()</strong></td><td>A reversed view of the list (Java 21)</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n</table>"
